        "html": "NIMC describes the NIN as a unique identifier assigned to an individual and used to establish identity across the national identity system.<br>Property doesn’t need anything resembling a NIN. But it can benefit from the same underlying principle: a fixed reference that stays constant while everything attached to it — ownership, documentation, use — keeps changing around it."
